</surname> <given-names>AE</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Invasive group A streptococcal infections in Ontario, Canada.</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source> <year>1996</year>;<volume>335</volume>:<fpage>547</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>54</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199608223350803</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8684408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R6"><label>6. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>O&#x02019;Loughlin</surname> <given-names>RE</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Roberson</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Cieslak</surname> <given-names>PR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lynfield</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Gershman</surname> <given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Craig</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>The epidemiology of invasive group A streptococcal infection and potential vaccine implications: United States, 2000&#x02013;2004.</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>853</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>62</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/521264</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17806049</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R7"><label>7. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Reid</surname> <given-names>RI</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Briggs</surname> <given-names>RS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Seal</surname> <given-names>DV</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Pearson</surname> <given-names>AD</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Virulent <italic>Streptococcus pyogenes</italic>: outbreak and spread within a geriatric unit.</article-title><source>J Infect</source> <year>1983</year>;<volume>6</volume>:<fpage>219</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>25</lpage> <p